⬇️FULL RECIPE⬇️
303 calories 32g protein (for the entire pint, mix-ins/toppings included)

Red Velvet Cake Protein Blizzard 😋🍦

Full recipe book (175+ flavors) in bio!

- 400g Fat Free High Protein Milk
- 22g (2 tbsp) whipped (or regular) cream cheese
- 40-45g Monk Fruit sweetener
- 5g (1 tsp) vanilla bean paste (or extract)
- A pinch of salt
- 1g (¼ tsp) xanthan gum
Mix-ins/toppings:
- ½ of a Red Velvet Prime Bites Protein Brownie (code FPF to save $$)
303 cal 18g C, 11g F, 32g P

Instructions:
1. Blend all ingredients for the base and freeze (at least 16 hours)
2. At the same time, chop the brownie into bite-sized cubes, place in a plastic bag, and put into the freezer. This allows it them firm up and withstand the power of the Mix-in setting (so they don’t get completely pulverized)
3. Run your pint under hot water for at least 60 seconds
4. Spin on “Lite Ice Cream” setting
5. Spin on “Respin” setting if very powdery
6. Make a hole down to the bottom with a butter knife and add the frozen brownie pieces
7. Run the “Mix-in” cycle

